## The bead, and what actually shipped against it

The bead: check (c) of the completeness audit counts `cadence-retro` **refs**,
while lanes write retro **markdown**. Two artifacts, no link, so the check can
pass with no retro written or warn with three.

Shipped: `etude retro capture` and `etude retro generate` write the retro body to
`<root>/.etude/retros/<retro-id>.md` and record it in the manifest as
`refs.retro_file`. The committed markdown is now an **output of the command that
writes the ref**, so the two come from one step instead of two remembered ones.
A body already inside `.etude/retros/` is recorded where it is rather than copied
under a second name.

This inverts the bead's suggested direction (it proposed capturing a ref when
markdown lands). Both plan-gate seats accepted the inversion; the reasoning is in
`plan.md` §"Why not the alternatives" — a sweep command that captures existing
markdown is still a second remembered step, i.e. the present bug with one more
subcommand.

**What this does not fix, stated plainly:** a lane that hand-writes
`.etude/retros/x.md` and never runs capture still produces no ref, and check (c)
still cannot see it. That half is `etude-24d`, filed at the plan gate as the
gate asked, and named in the shipped docs so no reader concludes the whole
symptom is closed. Check (c) itself is untouched and still WARN-only, per the
plan's scope boundary and `etude-9uf.4`'s reasoning.

