## Optionals NOT folded, and why

1. **Automate the partial-write cleanup** (implement gate 1, partially). The
   cleanup itself is folded; the **test** is not. Forcing a short write on a real
   file needs a filesystem seam this package does not have, and adding one to
   prove two lines costs more than it protects.
2. **Automate "unresolvable root fails before any ref is written"** (verify gate
   4). Reaching that failure specifically requires a repo where
   `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` fails while HEAD resolves — not a state a test
   can construct honestly. The guarantee rests on the code's first statement plus
   a manual check; disclosed in `verify.md`, not silent.
3. **Turn the cwd/store coupling into an assertion** (implement gate 3). Folded
   as a doc comment instead: `refstore.Store` exposes no repo path to compare
   against, so the assertion would have to shell out to `git rev-parse` on a path
   the interface does not carry.

